-- title:
--   A Čerednik–Drinfel'd family on the fine moduli scheme
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \ne r$, and $N$ is a nonzero natural number which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Base rings (group `DVR`).** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, `Onr` is a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism `Fr`, such that `Onr` is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal, every element of `Onr` satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ — so the residue ring $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ plays the role of an algebraic closure of $\mathcal O/\pi$ and `Fr` of a Frobenius lift. Finally `vdet` is a homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^{n}$; thus `vdet` is the valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion algebra and moduli (group `MOD`).** $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and is ramified at a finite place $v$ exactly when $r \in v$ or $\bar r \in v$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order. A fake elliptic curve over a commutative ring $S$ is here an abelian scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} S$ with a commutative relative group law, two-dimensional fibres, an action of $\Lambda$ compatible with the group law and satisfying the reduced-trace condition, and a level-$N$ subscheme. The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with its point assignment `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and $N$-level (isomorphism-invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n \ge 3$ is prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; the scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` is a fine moduli space for such curves equipped with a full level-$n$ structure, and $G$ is a group acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ over the base, with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$, such that `hρ` holds: $\rho$ preserves the structure morphism, twisting a full level structure by $\chi(g)$ amounts to composing its moduli point with $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$ in the precise sense of `IsLevelTwistAction`. The morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ lies over the base, is invariant under all $\rho(h)$, and sends the point of a curve with level-$n$ structure to the point of the underlying curve.
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner data on the moduli schemes (group `TOWER`, summarised here).** For every prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ there is a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `ptT`, a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with an extra $\ell$-level subgroup, together with two degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base which on points forget the extra level, respectively pass to the quotient by it. Morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over the base realise the Atkin–Lehner correspondences at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points.
--
--   **Definite quaternion algebra and the group $\tilde\Gamma$ (group `DEF`).** $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb Q$ are negative and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ is ramified exactly at $\bar r$; $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an idelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1, n_1)$ Eichler of level $Nr$, and $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; $v$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma_t \le \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]^{\times}$ consists exactly of the units which are local units of $R_1$ at every place $\ne v$. The hypothesis `hs` (four clauses, summarised here) provides, for each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a unit $s_\ell$ and an idele $sf_\ell$ whose components away from $r$ are $s_\ell$ and whose component at $r$ is $1$, such that the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1, \mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1))$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ is the intersection of $\Gamma_t$ with its conjugate by $s_\ell$. A unit $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **Reduction data at $r$ (group `RED`).** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and `coord` is an injective, additive, unital map $\Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ (Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$) which is multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product, has dense image modulo all powers of $r$, and computes reduced traces. Over the residue ring $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ there is a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of the group law of $A_0$ in two variables with $A_0$ a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$, and families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base with degrees `deg`. The clauses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) assert: each pair $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level; $e$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to multiplications, both up to powers of $r$; conversely, if $e_\gamma$ is a multiplication up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar; for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the endomorphisms $\mathrm{actEnd}$ and $\mathrm{varpiEnd}$ of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that every $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0(\varepsilon) = r^{k_\gamma} g \iota_0(\gamma) g^{-1}$; every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ admits a labelling $\Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ transporting it along $e$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; and every $r$-power isogeny pair preserving the level on a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e_\gamma$. Further, $R_2 \le R_1$ is an order with the property that $r$-power multiples of elements of $R_1$ lie in $R_2$, and $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ is a family over the base; the clauses `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) assert that each $\hat e_x$ is a homomorphism for the group law commuting with the $\Lambda$-action and preserving the level, that $\hat e$ is unital, multiplicative in the contravariant sense $\hat e_{xy} = \hat e_y \, \hat e_x$ and sends integers to multiplications, that $\hat e_{\bar x}\,\hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$, that $\hat e$ agrees with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$ up to powers of $r$, and a joint version of `hE2` realising both the $\Gamma_t$- and the $R_2$-families through one conjugator $g$.
--
--   **Special formal modules and the Drinfel'd side (group `DRIN`).** $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to \mathrm{Onr}$ is a ring map; $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ and of height $4$. `MD` is a moduli package for $r$ over `Onr` which is a Zariski sheaf, and $\eta$ assigns to every rigidified object over a $r$-nilpotent `Onr`-algebra a point of `MD`; the three clauses of `hη` state that on admissible rigidified objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies points exactly under isomorphism, that $\eta$ commutes with base change, and that every point of `MD` is, Zariski-locally on the base, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$. Moreover $E_0$ is an injective ring map from the centraliser of $\mathrm{actEnd}$ and $\mathrm{varpiEnd}$ of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is comparable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ up to a fixed power $r^{m}$ in both directions. The family `eD` gives, for every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, a map from the points of the functor $\mathcal G$ attached to `MD` to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum (a point of the formal upper half plane functor $\Omega$ over $K_0, \pi$); by `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` it is natural, bijective, compatible with the first leg, transforms the action of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ into the twisted action $\mathrm{IsTwistedAct}$, sends $\pi$-translation to the once-Frobenius-twisted leg with unchanged Deligne datum, and $\pi$-translates always exist.
--
--   **Glueing data (group `GLUE`).** A ring map $\kappa : \mathrm{Onr}/(\pi) \to \mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps, an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$; a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; and the Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ over the residue ring: a curve $A_{0w}$, morphisms $aw, aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$, together with $bw, bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ with $bw$ preserving the level, and `hJOINTw`, which for every injective $E_0$ as above produces one conjugator $g$ realising simultaneously all $e_\gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_t$) and the composite $aw \cdot bw$, the latter with $E_0(\varepsilon_w) = r^{k_w'} g\, \iota_0(\bar w)\, g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$ and the conjugator $g_0$ (group `XI`).** For every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ and every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, $\Xi$ assigns to each rigidified curve $(E,\varrho)$ — that is, a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a reduction $E_b$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$, a pullback $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue of $\psi$, and an $r$-power isogeny $\varphi : E_b \to A_b$ preserving the level — a point of $\mathcal G$ over $B$. The clauses `hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef` assert: over connected $B$ (every idempotent is $0$ or $1$) the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$; $\Xi$ is compatible with pullbacks of rigidified curves; $\Xi$ is unchanged under isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated comparison sense; and over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, if $E$ carries a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ via `coord`, then $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is computed by a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, a shift $j \le 1$, the rigidity transport condition `IsRigTransport` for $\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0$, admissibility of $t$ for the $j$-fold Frobenius-untwisted leg, and $\Xi(E,\varrho) = \langle \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi, \eta(t)\rangle$. Finally $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is such that `heqΓ` and `heqW` hold: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds, for some $c \in \mathbb Z$, to the action of $r^{c}\, g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$, and passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (over connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible) corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\, g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **Last hypothesis.** $2$ is a unit in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $v_0 := \mathrm{vdet}(g_0) \in \mathbb Z$ and, for an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, $\psi^{\circ} := \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v_0}$. Call a rigidified curve $(E,\varrho)$ over $(B,\psi^{\circ})$ *even* when the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is again $\psi^{\circ}$, and say it *has image* $(\psi, P)$, with $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$, when the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ carries $\mathrm{eD}(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ to $(\psi,P)$, i.e. $\psi$ is the Frobenius twist of the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0^{-1})$ and $P$ is the pullback of the Deligne datum of $\mathrm{eD}(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ along $g_0$.
--
--   Then there exist a group homomorphism $\tilde\theta : \Gamma_t \to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ which, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, maps a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ and an element $g \in G$ to a $B$-point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that the following sixteen statements hold.
--
--   (1) $\Theta_f$ is natural: for every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ between $\pi$-nilpotent algebras, $\Theta_f$ of the transported triple is the transport of $\Theta_f$ of the triple.
--
--   (2) For all $g, h \in G$, composing the point $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ with the automorphism $\rho(h)$ of $M$ gives $\Theta_f(x, g)$.
--
--   (3) For $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and pairs $x, x'$ (leg and Deligne datum) related by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, one has $\Theta_f(x', \tilde\theta(\gamma)\, g) = \Theta_f(x, g)$ for all $g \in G$.
--
--   (4) Infinitesimal lifting: for every surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $p : B \to B_0$ between $\pi$-nilpotent algebras with $B$ Noetherian whose kernel has square zero (any two elements killed by $p$ have product $0$), every triple $x_0$ over $B_0$ and every $B$-point $y$ of $M$ whose image under $p$ is $\Theta_f(x_0)$, there is a unique triple $x$ over $B$ with $p_*x = x_0$ and $\Theta_f(x) = y$.
--
--   (5) Geometric fibres: for every algebraically closed field $k$ over $\mathcal O$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $g' = \tilde\theta(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ under $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and with $\psi'(y) = \psi(\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(\gamma))} y)$ for every $y \in \mathrm{Onr}$ that is fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(z))}$ for all scalar $z \in \Gamma_t$ with $\tilde\theta(z) = 1$.
--
--   (6) Existence of transported levels: over a Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, for every $\psi$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$, every rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $\psi^{\circ}$ and every formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on $E$ via `coord`, there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ satisfying the normalised level transport condition `IsNormLevelTransport` for $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota$, `coord` and $P_0$ relative to $\varrho$.
--
--   (7) Uniqueness of transported levels: over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, any two full level-$n$ structures on $E$ satisfying that transport condition relative to the same $\varrho$ have the same underlying section.
--
--   (8) Existence of even pairs: over a Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, for every $\psi$ and every Deligne datum $P$ there are $E$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $\psi^{\circ}$ such that $(E,\varrho)$ is even with image $(\psi,P)$.
--
--   (9) Uniqueness of even pairs: over such a $B$, two even pairs $(E,\varrho)$, $(E',\varrho')$ with the same image $(\psi,P)$ admit an isomorphism $i : E \cong E'$ over the base compatible with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level (`IsoVia`), together with a comparison of the rigidifications: morphisms $ib$ on the reductions and $uA$ on the pullbacks of $A_0$, compatible with $gb$, $gA$ and the structure morphisms, for which $ib$, $\varrho'.\varphi$, $uA$ and $\varrho.\varphi$ agree after multiplication by suitable powers of $r$.
--
--   (10) Base change of even pairs: for an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ between Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent algebras and an even pair $(E,\varrho)$ over $B$ with image $(\psi,P)$, there are a fake elliptic curve $E'$ over $B'$ with a pullback morphism $g$ to $E$ along $\varphi$ and a rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to $(\varphi\circ\psi)^{\circ}$ pulling back from $\varrho$, such that $(E',\varrho')$ is even with image $(\varphi\circ\psi, \varphi_*P)$.
--
--   (11) Over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, if $(E,\varrho)$ is even with image $(\psi,P)$ and $P_n$ is a transported level-$n$ structure on $E$, then the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ is the moduli point $\mathrm{ptF}$ of $(E,P_n)$.
--
--   (12) Under the same hypotheses, the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ followed by $p$ is the coarse moduli point $\mathrm{pt}$ of $E$.
--
--   (13) Action of $\Gamma_t$ on even pairs: over a Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, given an even pair $(E,\varrho)$ with image $(\psi,P)$, an element $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and a pair $(\psi',P')$ obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, there is a rigidification $\varrho'$ of the same curve $E$ relative to $(\psi')^{\circ}$ such that $(E,\varrho')$ is even with image $(\psi',P')$, such that any transported levels $P_n$ for $\varrho$ and $P_n'$ for $\varrho'$ satisfy $P_n' = \mathrm{act}(\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma)))_* P_n$, and such that for every prime $\ell \ne r$ invertible in $B$ and every extra $\ell$-level $K_0$ on $A_0$ stable under $e_\gamma$, any two extra $\ell$-levels $C, C'$ on $E$ that correspond to $K_0$ through $\varrho$ and through $\varrho'$ respectively cut out the same points of $E$.
--
--   (14) Action of a general unit: over a Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, given an even pair $(E,\varrho)$ with image $(\psi,P)$, a further curve $E'$ with a rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to $\psi^{\circ}$, a unit $h$ and $c \in \mathbb Z$ such that $r^{c}\, g_0 \iota_0(h) g_0^{-1}$ carries $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ to $\Xi(E',\varrho')$, and a pair $(\psi'',P'')$ obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(h)$, there is a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ relative to $(\psi'')^{\circ}$ such that $(E',\varrho'')$ is even with image $(\psi'',P'')$ and such that for every prime $\ell \ne r$ invertible in $B$, every extra $\ell$-level $K_0$ on $A_0$ and any extra $\ell$-levels $C, C'$ on $E'$ corresponding to $K_0$ through $\varrho'$ and through $\varrho''$ respectively, $C$ and $C'$ cut out the same points of $E'$.
--
--   (15) $\pi$-translation: over a Noetherian connected $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, given an even pair $(E,\varrho)$ with image $(\psi,P)$, a curve $E'$ with a rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to some leg $\psi_1$, an integer $c$ and a point $y$ which is a $\pi$-translate of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ and from which the action of $r^{c}$ reaches $\Xi(E',\varrho')$, there is a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ relative to $(\mathrm{Fr}\text{-twist of }\psi)^{\circ}$ such that $(E',\varrho'')$ is even with image $(\mathrm{Fr}\text{-twist of }\psi,\,P)$.
--
--   (16) Isomorphisms over one leg: for an algebraically closed field $k$ over $\mathcal O$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a single leg $\psi$, Deligne data $P, P'$, even pairs $(E,\varrho)$ with image $(\psi,P)$ and $(E',\varrho')$ with image $(\psi,P')$, and an isomorphism $i : E \cong E'$ over the base compatible with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level, there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ such that the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$, such that for all transported levels $P_n$ on $E$ and $P_n'$ on $E'$ the image under $i$ of $\mathrm{act}(\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma)))_*P_n$ is $P_n'$, and such that for every prime $\ell \ne r$ invertible in $k$, every extra $\ell$-level $K_0$ on $A_0$ and all extra $\ell$-levels $C$ on $E$, $C'$ on $E'$ corresponding to $K_0$ through $\varrho$ and $\varrho'$ respectively, the statement that $i$ matches $C$ with $C'$ on points is equivalent to the statement that $K_0$ is stable under $e_\gamma$.
--
--   This is the assembly step of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd $p$-adic uniformisation on the fine moduli scheme of fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure: it converts the rigidification/Drinfel'd dictionary (the comparison maps $\Xi$, $\mathrm{eD}$ and the conjugator $g_0$) into a $\Gamma_t$-equivariant family $\Theta_f$ of $\pi$-nilpotent points of $M$, together with the transported level structures and the Atkin–Lehner and Hecke compatibilities needed later. It is used by the theorem that assembles the uniformisation statement with its tower and Atkin–Lehner clauses; the variant recorded here restates the curve-isomorphism clause over a single leg and assumes $2$ invertible in $\mathcal O$.
